The  chroot  service  module  for PAM chroots users into either a
predetermined directory or one derived from their home directory.
If a user’s home directory as specified in the structure returned
by contains the string the portion of the directory name  to  the
left of that string is used as the chroot directory, and the por‐
tion  to  the  right will be the current working directory inside
the chroot tree.  Otherwise, the directories specified by the and
options (see below) are used.  Do not hold user ID 0 exempt  from
the  chroot  requirement.  Report a failure if a chroot directory
could not be derived from the user’s home directory, and the  op‐
tion  was  not  specified.  Specify the directory to into after a
successful call.  Specify the chroot  directory  to  use  if  one
could  not be derived from the user’s home directory.  The module
